{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 was received as 0xff causing TRAP uart data mismatch and tohost FAIL 0xdead. ser_tx = send_pattern[0] is driven low during reset because line 114 uses send_pattern <= ~1 (LSB 0) instead of idle-high ~0. This false start misaligns the receiver so the real 0xa5 frame is missed and idle 0xff is captured.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -110,8 +110,8 @@
 		if (reg_div_we)
 			send_dummy <= 1;
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			send_dummy <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5 TRAP gone, checksum differs from 9e1b73c13d0a095f6b9512137fc937a720f9b8a80231ffc4b660d6d1459f6985"}

